{"id":442523568,"author":{"login":"sooperset","id":32061883,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMDYxODgz","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"node_id":"RE_kwDONYN7OM4aYF-w","tag_name":"v0.24.2","target_commitish":"545c31ca6f59eb772daebe484d4e6ab25e099d12","name":"v0.24.2","draft":false,"immutable":false,"prerelease":false,"created_at":"2026-11-12T03:43:30Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T05:14:25Z","published_at":"2026-11-12T05:14:25Z","assets":[],"body":"## 🔒 Security\n\n- **Project filter: epic and parent references.** With `JIRA_PROJECTS_FILTER` set, `jira_get_issue` no longer fetches an epic in a project outside the filter, and no longer returns that epic's name or key. Creating, updating or transitioning an issue now refuses a parent, epic link or issue link that points outside the filter. This closes a gap left by the 0.24.1 filter fix. Advisory: GHSA-qx5g-fhgg-wm59. Thanks to @zohuyhieuzo03 for the report.\n\n## ✨ Features\n\n- **Transitions: required fields and `update_data`.** `jira_get_transitions` can list the fields a transition screen requires (`expand_fields`), and `jira_transition_issue` accepts `update_data`, for example a worklog when the screen requires Time Spent (#1335). Thanks to @0w1afk.\n\n## Upgrade notes\n\n- With `JIRA_PROJECTS_FILTER` set, `jira_get_issue` makes one extra Jira API call when the issue has an epic link, to check the epic's project.\n","mentions_count":2}
